-      "question": "How do the original C Tcl 8.4–9.1 and Jim info complete workers classify the exact independently constructed String inputs for braced variables, arrays, expansion, malformed tails, continuations, line endings and scalar character NUL?",
-      "conclusion": "All six original version and main processes exit 0 with empty stderr; all 246 public catch statuses are 0. Complete results depend on the original selected worker. Four first-close braced-variable cases return 1 on C 8.4/8.5/8.6 and Jim but 0 on C 9.0/9.1. The two open expansion cases return 1 on C 8.4 and 0 on every other provider. Every C release reports the exact malformed closed-quote/closed-brace tails and terminal backslash complete, while Jim reports them incomplete. Open braced-variable/array, pending bare/comment backslash-LF and Jim-sugar cases return 0 on all C releases and 1 on Jim. The complete 41-row matrix includes the shared, Unicode, CR/LF and scalar-NUL controls. A complete result does not establish valid syntax, candidate-script execution or readable variable contents. Source excerpts identify counted object-worker routing separately from the strlen public C wrapper. Configured Document scanner correspondence requires its own software comparison; no such assertion is attached here. Lexer ParseIssueKind is the sole typed lexical/component issue producer and diagnostic-message owner. Configured Document and REPL completeness retain full source/channel/configuration; checked String adapters retain their actual selected worker purpose. The authored source comparisons keep all246 original fresh Unicode String rows separate from Document geometry and original object/header/entry authority. Whole-file analysis, per-item recovery, codegen span queries, indexed/untracked Server source, SslicTcl and Explorer consumers retain the actual supplied complete parser configuration and source channel. Genuine extracted body input is explicitly nested; unavailable completeness remains distinct from false. Module source currency and Native admission are independent of the original246 fresh Unicode String result observations. The original nested-call collector authenticates complete parent/child source geometry and full retained input/configuration before collecting written bracket substitutions. It requires selected expression roles only for actual braced operands containing command syntax. An unknown selected braced role remains unavailable, while a literal braced operand contributes no commands; lexical substitutions alone issue no dispatch or body-entry receipt.",
-      "scope": "Exact fixed ASCII LF original CLI probe, fresh String scalar-codepoint construction and public info complete catch/result observations on measured C 8.4.20, 8.5.19, 8.6.18, 9.0.4, 9.1.0 and Jim 0.84-9-g5bac7c9. Candidate strings are queried, never evaluated by the probe. Character NUL is constructed with format %c from scalar 0; request UTF8 hex/codepoints are input metadata and confer no raw C-string byte-source, generic counted-NUL or private String representation equivalence. Original version and main receipts are independent, with exact argv/cwd and explicit TCL_LIBRARY overlays. All 159 listed inputs match before/after; compiler, unlisted inherited environment, runtime shared-library provenance and a new compilation were not captured. The 31 independently verified physical-LF source excerpts explain selected original source behavior without attesting source-to-binary equivalence, internal handler/argv/header/cache/frame or entered candidate source. No Registry, compiler, Normal/effect/SSA/editor permission, BIG-IP result or Rust test success follows. The prelaunch request and its original wording/status remain unchanged; actual receipts establish only their measured public purpose. Current direct test attributes and real module parents attach these source/API contracts only. They do not certify an executable inventory, passed assertion, complete Native comparison or changed-current-image result. Each original provider answer and independently closed software command retains its exact input/channel/source purpose. Current direct Rust and Tokio test attributes and real module parents attach these source/API contracts only. They do not certify an executable inventory, passed assertion, complete Native comparison or changed-current-image result. Each original provider answer and independently closed software command retains its exact input/channel/source purpose.",
+      "document": "docs/design/analysis/name-resolution-proofs/namespace-original-deep-import-chain.md",
+      "problem_statement": "Can original command/procedure/ensemble introspection follow 200 imported bindings, including depths 63,64,65 and200, without a fixed64 hop truncation? What do actual providers report after source rename, an unrelated replacement at the vacated spelling, middle import replacement, source deletion/recreation and ensemble configuration through a deep import? Genuine generation/token lifetimes must not be replaced by textual spelling heuristics.",
+      "question": "How do original namespace origin, procedure args/body/default/invocation and supported ensemble queries behave across depths 63,64,65 and 200 after source rename, vacated replacement, middle replacement and deletion/recreation?",
+      "conclusion": "All five pinned C releases and current Jim complete the three procedure-chain setups with 200 namespace bindings. Public origin and invocation succeed at depths 63,64,65 and 200. C procedure args/body/default queries resolve the original procedure at those depths. After source rename and a new procedure at the vacated spelling, C deep imports report the moved origin and ORIGINAL; replacing the middle binding changes origin to n100 and returns REPLACED; deleting the source invalidates deep imports, and recreating its spelling does not revive them. Current Jim uses its scripted alias channel: initial origin/invocation succeeds at those depths, but args/body report that the alias is not a procedure and info default is unsupported. After source rename Jim observes the vacated replacement and returns VACATED; after deletion/recreation its alias target becomes RECREATED. Jim middle replacement also resolves n100. C8.5 through C9.1 additionally retain ensemble exists/map/invocation through all four depths, configuration via the deep import and source rename, while ensemble args remains a nonprocedure query. C8.4 lacks namespace ensemble; Jim rejects the measured create form and supports neither the measured exists nor configure form. Their failed ensemble setup rows remain purpose limitations, not successful chain observations. Every original process exits `0` with empty stderr and 95 public rows. The exact observations reject a 64-hop truncation for these successful purposes, but do not establish an arbitrary unbounded depth or private token/header identity. Two additional marked Runtime source definitions are registered through the actual parent test module. The public comparator selects546 original CASE rows from the unchanged six-provider probe, keeping24 metadata rows outside its comparison and explicit Jim distribution helper selection. A separate deliberately malformed software generation cycle checks terminal refusal without a partial query origin.",
+      "scope": "The immutable original ASCII LF source creates four independently named groups for rename/vacated replacement, middle replacement, deletion/recreation and ensemble queries. Depth samples are63,64,65 and 200. Every query records caught code and counted public result hex; mandatory setup rows gate each group, so unsupported C8.4/Jim ensemble setup cannot supply positive ensemble behavior. Version and executable queries are fresh public rows in each same original process; current Jim namespace origin/import helper bodies are independently returned by public info body. The listed 137 original CLI/header/static archive/configuration/source/distribution library inputs remain exact before and after. No new compile, private command token, object/header/cache, compiled opcode or Native frame is sampled. Twenty-three exact original source windows explain C original-command/procedure/namespace/ensemble routes and Jim scripted helper/alias behavior separately from observed public results. Recorded absolute paths, explicit TCL_LIBRARY overlays and original launch arguments are retained; compiler version, unlisted inherited environment and unrelated system libraries are unrecorded. Generic aliases, invocation identity, future lookup, handler entry, Normal beyond each caught query, editor equivalence and BIG-IP do not follow. Existing two-hop and other original records remain unchanged. Runtime traversal tests and current source contracts require independent software receipts; publication supplies no backend assertion PASS. Module registration establishes source reachability only, not an executable inventory, launched assertion or passing comparison. The original six processes,570 raw rows and all provider answers remain unchanged. The software cycle has no Native counterpart, and Jim scripted alias observations cannot become200 genuine C-style Imported generations or private token/header identity. No arbitrary-depth, frame, handler or edit authority follows.",
